On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:32:30 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Of course I know I can type -inbox, but I want to know if that status
> will get synced to Fastmail. Otherwise it might just pick it up again.

It will not reach Fastmail, and it would not last even locally. A
notmuch tag lives only in the notmuch database. With flag sync on,
notmuch mirrors five tags to maildir flags (draft, flagged, passed,
replied, and unread), and inbox is not one of them. Our configs keep
flag sync off anyway.

It also comes back sooner than a rebuild. The post-new hook,
dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh, puts +inbox on every message from
someone else that you have not replied to, on every notmuch new. So
-inbox is undone by the next notmuch new. The same problem came up on
the jj maildir in "[PATCH 0/2] Archive from notmuch-emacs with the
archive tag" [1].

> Basically I'm trying to devise a workflow, and find a spot in between
> inbox and archive. I guess that doesn't make a whole lot of sense
> though...

It makes sense, and the synced maildir makes it cheap: the spot is a
folder. lab-mail's mbsync syncs every folder of the account (Patterns
*), and a folder you create on Fastmail or on lab-mail appears on the
other side within a minute. So INBOX, a folder such as "Later", and
Archive give you three states. Each lives in the list data, so
Fastmail, every client, and every agent sees the same state.

> In any case, what options are there for removing the inbox tag, and
> having that persist? I don't want messages to be tagged with inbox again
> if I re-create the database.

These are the options I found. Only the first two survive a rebuild
and reach Fastmail.

Option 1: Move the message to another folder (recommended). Archive is
already the design in lab-mail's spec.org ("Archive by folder, not by a
notmuch tag on beastie"), and an in-between folder works the same way.
For this to persist, mail-tag.sh must give inbox only to messages in
INBOX, e.g. "folder:INBOX and not (me) and not replied", and tag the
other folders by name, e.g. +later for folder:Later and +archived for
folder:Archive. It needs two changes. The hook change is small, and
beastie's mbsync must push moves to lab-mail, with Expunge Both, as
lab-mail's spec.org says. The earlier client spec, "[PATCH]
dotfiles/notmuch: Spec reading and sending through lab-mail" [2], made
beastie pull-only, so a move there would be undone by the next pull. In
Emacs, archiving then moves the file rather than changing a tag, as
"[PATCH] emacs: Archive notmuch mail by moving its file" [3] did for the
jj maildir.

Option 2: Use an IMAP flag. \Flagged travels both ways through mbsync
and Fastmail, and with synchronize_flags=true it becomes the flagged
tag. The hook could then leave flagged mail out of the inbox. This
avoids a folder, but it overloads "flagged", turns on file renames on
every client, and adds unread tags everywhere. I would not pick it.

Option 3: Keep the tags out of band, with notmuch dump/restore or
notmuch-git(1), as researched in "find info on notmuch-git(1) and how
notmuch list uses notmuch" [4]. This survives a rebuild if you keep the
dump, but it never reaches Fastmail and no agent sees it. The hook would
still have to stop re-adding inbox.

If you want option 1, tell me the name of the in-between folder and
I will send a patch to mail-tag.sh and to beastie's mbsync config. I
have not sent one yet, because the folder names are yours to choose
and the hook change would also change what the agents see as inbox.

